er (FAT, DIFAT and miniFAT).\n  - `msi_name()` decodes the mangled stream names (0x3800–0x4840 base-64 packing).\n  - `msi_property()` reads the StringPool header (codepage, with string refs 3 bytes wide if bit 0x80000000 is set, else 2), builds the string list (long-string escape when length is 0), then reads the column-major `!Property` table: all keys first, then all values.\n- Fallback in the solver: regex `ProductCode(\\{[0-9A-Fa-f-]{36}\\})` over the raw bytes.\n\n**4. GM spelling conventions**\nThe format text says \"canonical GUID text in 8-4-4-4-12 hexadecimal form, including hyphens\", with normalization `trim`. Despite that wording, the GM wants braces.\n\n| Mode | answer_id | Confirmed value |\n|---|---|---|\n| single | `d13-msi-001-msi-product-code-guid` | `{DD1A80D5-0250-4F4D-B289-13096D633C61}` |\n| TT | `d13-msi-002-msi-product-code-guid` | `{DD1A80D5-0250-4F4D-B289-13096D633C61}` |\n| mastery | `set1.d13-msi-003-msi-product-code-guid` | `{DD1A80D5-0250-4F4D-B289-13096D633C61}` |\n| mastery | `set2.d13-msi-004-msi-product-code-guid` | `{DD1A80D5-0250-4F4D-B289-13096D633C61}` |\n\n- **Rejected:** `single_solve/submissions.jsonl` at ts 20261013T130106Z shows `\"DD1A80D5-0250-4F4D-B289-13096D633C61\"` with kind=incorrect.\n- **Accepted:** at 130125Z the braced form came back kind=correct, CORRECT, flag `ea4047d4b274edcfcbb88c7afe1a3568`.\n- Uppercase was the only case tried and is the case MSI stores, so lowercase is untested.\n\n**5. Pitfalls and time lost**\n- The only mistake was stripping the braces (the solver's `_guid()` returned `group(1)`) because the format text didn't mention them. It cost one incorrect submission and about 19 seconds.\n- `_guid()` now returns `\"{%s}\" % guid.upper()`, and `NOTES.md` records this as a lib/vocab rule.\n- No other errors.\n\n**6. Time from start to CORRECT**\nStart 13:00:08.842Z, artifact downloaded 13:00:11, incorrect at 13:01:06, CORRECT at 13:01:25.052Z. That is about 76 seconds.\n\n**7. TT and mastery outcomes**\n- **TT:** correct on the first submit at 13:01:35, flag `d0b7266c7535a452da677839a0ad7812`. Window 50 s, elapsed 1.68 s, 0.96 s inside the window. Not Hall of Fame eligible, 0 attempts remaining.\n- **Mastery:** correct on the first submit at 13:01:40, flag `484a2034c43a1a95976a623bafe420cc`. Window 80 s, elapsed 4.36 s, 2.55 s inside the window. Not Hall of Fame eligible, 0 attempts remaining.\n- Both were solved by `solve.py` with no failures.\n\n**8. Variant axes (single vs TT vs mastery)**\n- The question kind is the same everywhere: `msi.product_code_guid`, pattern format, trim. The other things the prompt hints at (UpgradeCode, revision, collision) never became questions here.\n- Only the installer number and filenames change:\n  - single: `installer-001.msi` (sha256 `7e614b47…`)\n  - TT: `installer-002.msi` (sha256 `9ed8794c…`, different bytes, same size 9728)\n  - mastery: one bundle zip (sha256 `1c2e207f…`) containing `metadata-day-13-evidence-01.zip -> installer-003.msi` (set1) and `-02.zip -> installer-004.msi` (set2)\n- Mastery ids carry a `setN.` prefix.\n- All four installers have the same ProductCode, `{DD1A80D5-…}`. That is the \"collision\": the files are repackaged copies of one product, so their bytes differ but the identity doesn't.\n- Parse rule in `solve.py`: take the text after `-msi-` in the id tail and drop any trailing `-guid`. Map `product-code`, `upgrade-code`, `product-version`, `product-name`, `manufacturer` and `product-language` to their Property names. Return the Property value, wrapped by `_guid()` (braced, uppercase) when the id contains `guid`.\n\nFiles are in `/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/challenges/day13/metadata-product-placement/`:\n- `solver/solve.py`\n- `solver/NOTES.md`\n- `single_solve/submissions.jsonl`\n- `single_solve/worker-single-local-20261013T210007.log`\n- `time_trial/last_timed.json`\n- `mastery/last_timed.json`\n- `solver/cases/{single_solve,auto-time_trial-e274e977,auto-mastery-7f347235}/`"}],"container":n