{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bvw24ZCpgSq7x2hvTVkd5F","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-12; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n5\t  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n6\t- Every day = ONE evidence zip (`metadata-day-NN-evidence.zip`, plain Deflate, no password so far). Days 1-7: one tiny\n7\t  member (33 B - 3 KB) and ONE structural fact. Day 8+: the zip carries the whole cumulative kit (note + jpg + png + pdf +\n8\t  inner zip [+ D9 a 1.26 MB PE `.exe`]) and even the SINGLE contract asks every field (D8 12, D9 13 = identity + every\n9\t  earlier day's field + the new one). The member can itself be a container (D7/8: an inner ZIP whose own EOCD / CD is\n10\t  the asked field). Each day adds ONE member + ONE field; the previous kit members are byte-identical except the case id.\n11\t- Day 9 crossed into EXECUTABLE headers (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`): the metadata lane now parses binaries too, but only\n12\t  the raw header field -- answer the u16 as hex, not the binary lane's machine word (`i386`). Day 10 stayed on the SAME\n13\t  PE (`pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex`) and DE-escalated: zip = the exe only, contract = 1 field (TT 1, Mastery 2x1).\n14\t  Day 11 kept that shape and moved INTO the PE's resources (`pe.version_original_filename`, VS_VERSIONINFO string).\n15\t  Day 12 switched to a NEW member family -- a 5 KB .NET dll (`d12-dotnet-NNN-dotnet-mvid-guid`) -- and went into the CLI\n16\t  METADATA tables (Module.Mvid via the #GUID heap); same 1-field / TT 1 / Mastery 2x1 shape.\n17\t- A new `<fmt>.<field>` family each day: identity (name/size/hashes) -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` ->\n18\t  `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` -> `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries` ->\n19\t  `zip.central_directory_member_names` -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` ->\n20\t  `pe.version_original_filename` -> `dotnet.mvid_guid`. Since Day 3 the question literally names the field\n21\t  (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); answer ids read `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`). NOTE the\n22\t  `dNN` is the drop/member family, not the day the field appeared: Day 8's new field came as `d07-zip-001-zip-central-\n23\t  directory-member-names`; Day 9's as `d09-pe-001-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex` (new member family -> new `dNN`); Day 10's as `d09-pe-001-pe-address-of-entry-point-rva-hex` (same exe family), Day 11's as\n24\t  `d09-pe-001-pe-version-original-filename`, Day 12's as `d12-dotnet-001-dotnet-mvid-guid` (new family -> new `dNN`).\n25\t- The prompt's flavor text describes decoys (impostors, renamed copies, \"-with-bom\" names, EXIF/presentation lies, chunk\n26\t  \"passengers\", catalog /Version overrides, \"impossible provenance\" names). The asked field so far was always the\n27\t  STRUCTURAL truth from the header/record bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. Singles D1-D9 were\n28\t  first-submit CORRECT in ~27-60 s; D10 took one wrong spelling (unpadded hex). Every TT/Mastery since D4 CORRECT first try.\n29\t- The flavor promises MORE than the sample delivers (D9: \"executables for several architectures, plus decoys wearing\n30\t  executable extensions\" -> one honest i386 PE, no ELF/Mach-O/decoy in any mode). Expect the promised cases to arrive\n31\t  later as mutations; pre-arm the sibling parsers (ELF/Mach-O/decoy -> `none`) without guessing their spellings.\n32\t- Titles are puns, not format hints: Day 7 \"Seven-Zip, No Relation\" was plain ZIP (PKWARE), no .7z anywhere.\n33\t\n34\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n35\t- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\" below; resolve the named member through whatever wrapper arrives.\n36\t- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions/names, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree\n37\t  with the header: always answer from the structural header bytes of the member the question names.\n38\t- **Member and values** -- names, sizes, dimensions and counts re-roll per variant; nothing about the sample is\n39\t  constant (Day 7 entry count went 2/3/4/5 with drop number 001-004; member names `room-NN/item-K.txt`). Day 8 re-rolled\n40\t  ONLY the note's case id (`Case <hex> evidence note.`, 33 B) -> md5/sha1/sha256/magic differ per set; jpg 257x146, png\n41\t  269x153, pdf 1.4, eocd 2, CD names identical across single/TT/5 Mastery sets. D9 same, plus the PE: Machine 0x014c in\n42\t  all 7 copies but the exe's sha256 differs per set (re-built per variant). D10: the entry RVA re-rolled per variant\n43\t  (single 0x00065bd0, TT 0x00063a80, Mastery 0x00063510 / 0x00065bd0). D11: the PE's ARCHITECTURE re-rolled per variant\n44\t  (single 386 0x014c, TT amd64 0x8664, Mastery arm64 0xaa64 + 386) and OriginalFilename follows it (`pe-base-<goarch>.exe`).\n45\t  D12: every dll is 5,120 B with the same layout; the MVID, the sha256 and the `Huntress.Managed.<12HEX>` type name re-roll\n46\t  per variant (managed-001..004).\n47\t  Never cache a value across sets.\n48\t- **Field-set size** -- grows AND shrinks: D7 TT/Mastery went 1 -> 11 fields (Mastery 22); D8 12 in every mode (Mastery\n49\t  5 x 12); D9 13 (Mastery 5 x 13); D10 back to ONE field everywhere (Mastery 2 sets x 1, zip = the lone exe). Families: the day's field +\n50\t  `evidence-note-{filename,size-bytes,md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}` + carry-overs\n51\t  `d04-jpeg-*-sof-dimensions-pixels`, `d05-png-*-ihdr-dimensions-pixels`, `d06-pdf-*-header-version`, `d07-zip-*-eocd-\n52\t  total-entries`, `d07-zip-*-central-directory-member-names`, `d09-pe-*-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex`. Dispatch on the\n53\t  answer-id SUFFIX and keep EVERY earlier family answerable (reference: `challenges/day09/metadata-built-different/\n54\t  solver/solve.py` answers all 13; `day10/metadata-where-do-we-begin/solver/solve.py` = those + entry/image-base/opt-magic\n55\t  /ELF e_entry branches).\n56\t- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes, case-insensitive; D9 also `0x`-hex with `trim` only,\n57\t  so case MATTERS -> lowercase), `enum` (`accepted_values`), and since D8 `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact\n58\t  values and order\"). Emit per `answer_format.kind`; read `syntax` for prefix/case (`0x` yes for u16_hex, no for magic).\n59\t- **Question-text tags** (D9 TT/Mastery, new): the first question gets ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<64 hex>]` appended\n60\t  (Mastery: the bundle's sha, same for every set). Strip `\\s*\\[[^\\]]*\\]$` before reading a member name from question\n61\t  text; route by `answer_id` + `artifact` instead (the D9 solver was unaffected for that reason).\n62\t- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7: outer -> `...-evidence-0N.zip` ->\n63\t  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer from an enclosing zip.\n64\t\n65\t## Recognition cues -> first move\n66\t| You see | First move |\n67\t|---|---|\n68\t| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | `7z l -slt <zip>` then `7z x -o work/ <zip>`; (or python `zipfile` read of the member) |\n69\t| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the extracted member (bytes, not the zip entry name) |\n70\t| \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |\n71\t| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM = `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`, UTF-32LE `ff fe 00 00`) -> `true`/`false` |\n72\t| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk JPEG segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width. `exiftool -ImageSize` cross-check only |\n73\t| `png.ihdr_*` / \"walk their chunks\" | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = IHDR width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC loop (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n74\t| `zip.eocd_*` / \"count what the archives claim\" | of the NAMED inner zip (not the evidence zip): last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+8 disk entries, @+10 total, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset, u16 @+20 comment len. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 locator `PK\\x06\\x07` (EOCD-20) -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32. Cross-check: count `PK\\x01\\x02` walking from cd offset, `PK\\x03\\x04` |\n75\t| `zip.central_directory_*` / \"inventory every stored path, preserve directory context\" | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from EOCD cd-offset (fallback `EOCD - cd_size` if data prepended): name len u16 @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name at +46; next = +46+n+e+c. Raw stored path, CD order, no basename/dedupe/sort; decode UTF-8 (flag bit 11 `0x800`, else try UTF-8 then cp437). `7z l -slt` / `zipinfo -1` as cross-check |\n76\t| `pdf.header_version` / \"declared versions\" | `head -c 16 <f> | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; `grep -a -o '/Version[^/>]*'` only as a diagnostic |\n77\t| `pe.coff_*` / \"executables for several architectures\", `.exe`/`.dll`/`.sys` | `MZ`@0 -> e_lfanew u32 LE @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` there -> COFF FileHeader: Machine u16 @+4, NumberOfSections @+6, TimeDateStamp @+8, SizeOfOptionalHeader @+20, Characteristics @+22; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b` PE32 / `0x20b` PE32+). `xxd -s $((0x3c)) -l 4` then `xxd -s <lfanew> -l 8`. `file`/`pefile` cross-check only |\n78\t| `pe.address_of_entry_point_*` / `pe.image_base*` / \"start addresses\" | opt = e_lfanew+24: AddressOfEntryPoint u32 @opt+16 (an RVA); ImageBase u32 @opt+28 (PE32) / u64 @opt+24 (PE32+). `od -An -tx4 -j$((lfanew+40)) -N4 f`. objdump's \"start address\" = ImageBase+RVA (a VA, NOT the RVA) |\n79\t| `elf.*` / `macho.*` siblings (promised \"several architectures\", not yet asked) | ELF: `\\x7fELF`, EI_DATA @5 picks endianness, e_machine u16 @18. Mach-O: `feedface`/`feedfacf` (either byte order) cputype u32 @4; fat `cafebabe` = BE nfat_arch @4 + 20-B entries (Java .class shares `cafebabe`; small nfat_arch = fat). Emit hex in the same `0x%0Nx` width as the field's `uNN` |\n80\t| `dotnet.*` / `.dll` \"Mono/.Net assembly\" / \"module identities\", \"rebuilds vs renames\" | CLI metadata, stdlib only (no dnfile in-window): PE data dir 14 (CLI header) -> MetaData RVA -> `BSJB` root -> stream headers (`#~`, `#Strings`, `#GUID`, `#Blob`). `#~`: HeapSizes byte @+6 (bit1 = 4-byte GUID index), Valid u64 @+8, row counts @+24; Module row 0 = Generation u16, Name (str idx), **Mvid (guid idx, 1-based)** -> 16 B at #GUID+(i-1)*16 -> `str(uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..))`. Cross-check: `monodis`/`ilspycmd -il` print `.module` + `// MVID: {..}` |\n81\t| `pe.version_*` / \"version resources remember what the binaries called themselves\" | VS_VERSIONINFO StringFileInfo: `pefile.PE(data=b, fast_load=True)`; `pe.parse_data_directories(directories=[DIRECTORY_ENTRY['IMAGE_DIRECTORY_ENTRY_RESOURCE']])`; walk `pe.FileInfo[..][..].StringTable[..].entries` (bytes keys). Match the id tail to the key ignoring case/`-_` (`original-filename` -> `OriginalFilename`). Shell: `strings -e l f.exe | grep -A1 OriginalFilename` |\n82\t| exe-extension decoy (`.exe` that is text/zip/PNG, `MZ` with no/garbled `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | header absent -> literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit or the extension |\n83\t| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n84\t| answer_format syntax \"use the literal none only when the requested field is absent\" | field missing (e.g. no header) -> `none` |\n85\t| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)` -- compact, no spaces, no Markdown |\n86\t| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids, artifact `delivery N: <zip> -> <member>` or `<zip>-0N.zip -> <member>` | resolve each set's member separately; see delivery layouts below |\n87\t\n88\t## Day by day\n89\t**Day 1 — You Must Be This Hash to Ride** (identity: filename / size-bytes / md5 / sha1 / sha256 via `zipfile` +\n90\t`hashlib`; CORRECT ~36 s). Mastery zip-of-zips first seen.\n91\t\n92\t**Day 2 — Looks Can Be Deceiving** (`magic-prefix-hex-16`: first 16 bytes, lowercase hex, no `0x`; ~34 s). TT `readme.exe`\n93\twas text, Mastery `.bin` was a PDF. TT question text named a member that didn't exist -> `lib.common.find_artifact_hinted`;\n94\tzip-of-zips broke name lookup -> `find_artifact` recurses nested zips.\n95\t\n96\t**Day 3 — BOM Voyage** (`text.utf8_bom_present` enum `true`/`false`). First 3 bytes == `EF BB BF`; CORRECT ~28 s.\n97\tMastery `export-001-with-bom.txt` really had a BOM -- decide from bytes, never the name. utf16/32 variants unconfirmed.\n98\t\n99\t**Day 4 — Picture This** (`jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels`). Walk segments by declared length to SOFn (one SOF0 @0x88) ->\n100\t`<width>x<height>` (GM-confirmed; not EXIF/filename dims). Rotation flavor not asked. CORRECT ~38 s; TT/Mastery in-window.\n101\t\n102\t**Day 5 — Chunk Norris** (`png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels`). IHDR @0x10 BE u32 width,height -> `<width>x<height>` (Day 4\n103\tform by analogy, accepted). IDAT/CRC/after-IEND \"passenger\" checks were diagnostics only. CORRECT ~33 s, first try.\n104\t\n105\t**Day 6 — Portable Deception** (`pdf.header_version`): `xxd -l 16` -> `%PDF-1.4` -> bare `x.y` (~34 s). Adopted, not\n106\tGM-judged: header must be at offset 0 (deeper `%PDF-` -> `none`); catalog `/Version` never changes it. Mastery: two\n107\tsame-named downloads (`delivery N:` refs); pre-fetched contract listed 003/004, live asked 006/007.\n108\t\n109\t**Day 7 — Seven-Zip, No Relation** (`zip.eocd_total_entries` integer of the INNER `evidence-drop-001.zip`): EOCD u16\n110\t@+10 = `2` (the claim; all variants honest, claim-vs-walk disagreement never exercised). Stdlib `struct` EOCD parser,\n111\t57 s first try; TT 3 entries, Mastery 4 / 5.\n112\t\n113\t**Day 8 — What's in the Box?** (`zip.central_directory_member_names`, kind `json`): 5-member kit (note/jpg/png/pdf/D7\n114\tinner zip), single = 12 fields. Inner zip's CD names verbatim in CD order, full paths (basenames collide):\n115\t`[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]`, compact JSON. \"Impossible provenance\" decoy unexercised. ~27 s first try.\n116\t\n117\t**Day 9 — Built Different** (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`, `pattern` lowercase `0x`): kit + `telemetry-agent-001.exe`, an\n118\thonest Go 1.22 386 PE32 (e_lfanew 0x80, 7 sections, opt magic 0x10b). COFF Machine u16 -> `0x014c` (padded; not `i386`,\n119\tthe binary lane's word). \"Several architectures + decoys\" flavor unexercised. ~47 s first try; TT/Mastery 5 x 13 in-window.\n120\t\n121\t**Day 10 — Where Do We Begin?** (`pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex`, id `d09-pe-001-...`): zip = the D9 Go 386 PE\n122\talone, 1 field everywhere. OptionalHeader.AddressOfEntryPoint (u32 @ e_lfanew+40) `0x%08x` -> `0x00065bd0`; unpadded\n123\t`0x65bd0` REJECTED (lane's first wrong submit). objdump's start address is the VA, not the RVA. ~75 s, 1 wrong; TT/Mastery\n124\tfirst try (RVA re-rolled per variant). \"Lying report\" flavour unexercised.\n125\t\n126\t**Day 11 — What's My Name Again?** (`pe.version_original_filename`, id `d09-pe-001-pe-version-original-filename`): same\n127\tlone Go PE; VS_VERSIONINFO OriginalFilename VERBATIM (`pe-base-386.exe`), not the randomized member name\n128\t(`telemetry-agent-001.exe` = the \"impersonator\"). pefile resource walk, ONE command, ~25 s first try; TT amd64 / Mastery\n129\tarm64 + 386 variants, both first try.\n130\t\n131\t**Day 12 — Managed Expectations** (`dotnet.mvid_guid`, kind `pattern`, syntax \"canonical GUID text in 8-4-4-4-12\n132\thexadecimal form, including hyphens\", norm `trim`, id `d12-dotnet-001-dotnet-mvid-guid`). Prompt: \"The .NET assemblies\n133\tshare names, versions, and source ancestry -- but their module identities remain distinct. Separate rebuilds from renames.\"\n134\t- Artifact: 2 KB zip -> `managed-001.dll`, 5,120 B PE32 i386 .NET (BSJB `v4.0.30319`; `<Module>`, a\n135\t  `Huntress.Managed.<12HEX>` type and a `get_ModuleVersionId` memberref -- the hint). One dll per delivery; the \"renames vs\n136\t  rebuilds\" comparison was never asked, only the MVID.\n137\t- Key insight: MVID = Module table row 0, 3rd column (guid-heap index, 1-based) -> 16 bytes in `#GUID` rendered as .NET\n138\t  `Guid.ToString()` = mixed-endian (`uuid.UUID(bytes_le=...)`), lowercase, no braces: `21e410f3-c977-465c-80eb-6890ddd3085c`.\n139\t- Worker: the solver was the bare skeleton; it typed a ~90-line stdlib PE -> CLI header -> BSJB streams -> `#~` -> `#GUID`\n140\t  parser + the old identity/PE branches and submitted in ONE command (2 tool calls; most of the ~55 s launch->CORRECT was\n141\t  generation). First try. Reference parser: `challenges/day12/metadata-managed-expectations/solver/solve.py` `dotnet_mvid`.\n142\t- TT window 30 s, in_window 0.95 s (managed-002); Mastery 2 sets (003/004), in_window 1.5 s. Both CORRECT first try.\n143\t\n144\t## GM answer conventions learned\n145\t- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n146\t- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`).\n147\t- Booleans: enum `true` / `false` (lowercase) — the contract hands the vocabulary; pick, don't probe.\n148\t- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR): `<width>x<height>` — width first, lowercase `x`, no spaces (GM-confirmed both,\n149\t  re-confirmed D8 `257x146` / `269x153`).\n150\t- PDF header version: bare `x.y` from the leading `%PDF-x.y` (no `PDF-`/`%` prefix); absent header -> literal `none`\n151\t  (contract wording; `none` itself not yet GM-confirmed).\n152\t- Counts (`zip.eocd_total_entries`): plain base-10 integer string, e.g. `2` (GM-confirmed D7 + D8 all modes).\n153\t- JSON lists (`zip.central_directory_member_names`): compact array, no spaces after `,`, double quotes, full stored path\n154\t  with `/` dirs, CD order -- `[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]` (GM-confirmed D8 single/TT/Mastery x5).\n155\t  Whether the GM's `trim` normalization also tolerates `\", \"` spacing is untested -- always emit compact.\n156\t- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 Machine ->\n157\t  `0x014c` (D9), u32 AddressOfEntryPoint -> `0x00065bd0` (D10, all modes). The width comes from the STRUCT, not the id\n158\t  (D10's id has no `u32`). Contrast: magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; binary-lane `machine` wants the word (`i386`), and the\n159\t  binary lane's `entry_point` was accepted UNPADDED (`0x401040`) -- different lane, different generator.\n160\t- GUIDs (`dotnet.mvid_guid`): .NET `Guid.ToString()` form -- first 3 groups byte-swapped from the heap bytes (bytes_le),\n161\t  lowercase, hyphenated, no braces (D12 all modes; `knowledge.DOTNET_MVID_GUID`, playbook metadata `guid` entry).\n162\t- Version-resource strings (`pe.version_<field>`): the StringFileInfo value verbatim, incl. extension (`pe-base-386.exe`,\n163\t  D11 all modes). `knowledge.PE_VERSION_STRING_KEY` maps id tail -> resource key.\n164\t- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` for pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex (D10 single; unpadded) -- the only one, days 1-12.\n165\t- `knowledge.py`: `JPEG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PNG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PDF_HEADER_VERSION_FMT`, `ZIP_EOCD_TOTAL_ENTRIES_FMT`,\n166\t  `ZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_FMT`, `PE_COFF_MACHINE_U16_HEX_FMT`, `PE_ENTRY_POINT_RVA_HEX_FMT` (+`_REJECTED`), `BOOL`;\n167\t  `playbook` metadata `hex` entry carries the padding rule.\n168\t- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_dimensions_pixels` = SOF frame header, `ihdr_` = IHDR chunk,\n169\t  `header_version` = file header, `eocd_total_entries` = EOCD record's own claim, `central_directory_member_names` = CD\n170\t  file-name fields, `coff_machine_u16_hex` = COFF FileHeader.Machine as u16 hex) — read the field name literally to\n171\t  pick which structure to parse; a claimed count is NOT a CD walk / `zipfile` len, and CD names are NOT local-header\n172\t  names (they happened to agree on D7/D8). A `_uNN_hex` suffix fixes both the read width and the printed width.\n173\t\n174\t## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n175\t- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (D8: 5 members, filename question's artifact = zip only).\n176\t- Mastery days 1,2,4,5: ONE download named `...-evidence-01.zip` that is an outer zip containing `...-01.zip` and\n177\t  `...-02.zip` (zip-of-zips); each inner zip holds its set's member.\n178\t- Mastery day 7: zip-of-zips again, three levels (outer `-01.zip` holds `-01.zip` + `-02.zip`, each holding the asked\n179\t  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); artifact ref `metadata-day-07-evidence-0N.zip -> evidence-drop-00N.zip` (no `delivery N:`).\n180\t- Mastery day 8: same shape, FIVE sets: one 17 KB download `metadata-day-08-evidence-01.zip` (Stored, UTF-8 flag) holding\n181\t  `-01.zip`..`-05.zip`, each a full 5-member kit (incl. its own `evidence-drop-001.zip`). Refs `...-evidence-0N.zip ->\n182\t  <member>`; every set reuses the same member names, so resolve by (set zip, member), never member name alone.\n183\t- Mastery day 9: same five-set shape, but the GM download is named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip`\n184\t  (`metadata-forensics-day-09-built-different-mastery.zip`, 2.99 MB, Stored) while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip\n185\t  -> <member>` -- resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not by its filename.\n186\t- Mastery day 10: TWO sets only, refs `metadata-day-10-evidence-0N.zip -> telemetry-agent-00N.exe` (003/004).\n187\t  Day 11 identical shape (`metadata-day-11-evidence-0N.zip`, one download nesting both set zips).\n188\t- Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` in artifact refs.\n189\t- Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) — never hardcode names.\n190\t\n191\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n192\t- Name lookup by zip filename alone breaks on zip-of-zips (returned `PK` bytes as the \"magic\") — recurse into nested zips.\n193\t- Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (Day 2 TT): answer under `answer_ids`, locate the member that exists.\n194\t- Don't let the flavor text widen the question: prompts mention impostors/passengers/orientation/provenance, but only the\n195\t  named field is graded. Answer it; keep extra checks as diagnostics.\n196\t- Container-of-containers: when the asked file is itself a zip, a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded evidence\n197\t  zip reads the OUTER EOCD / CD (D8 outer CD = the 5 kit members, Mastery outer = 5 set zips). Resolve the named member's\n198\t  bytes first, then parse.\n199\t- Name-list fields: `zipfile.namelist()` is CD order but decodes non-UTF-8-flagged names as cp437 and is fine for honest\n200\t  zips; for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `C:\\`, `\\` separators, LFH != CD name, duplicates) emit the CD bytes as-is --\n201\t  don't let an extractor's sanitizing (7z/unzip strip `../` and leading `/`) rewrite the answer.\n202\t- Decoys by name: `*-with-bom.txt`, `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF, `.pdf` that is PNG — bytes win every time.\n203\t- Timed windows are ~5-10 s (D8: TT 8 s / Mastery 10 s; D9 shrank to 6 s / 7 s) and most of it is GM start/download/\n204\t  submit round-trips (D9 TT submit alone 2.3 s): never do anything slow (extraction to disk, exiftool, `pefile` full\n205\t  parse, subprocess) in-window; parse fixed offsets in memory. Big members (1.2 MB exe x5) pushed Mastery solve to 0.86 s\n206\t  -- decompress each member once and cache by (set zip, member).\n207\t- Fresh member family = skeleton solver (D10, D12): copy the previous day's solver first, then add the new family's\n208\t  handler -- D12's worker re-typed the identity/PE branches next to the .NET parser (~50 s of generation).\n209\t- Executable fields: don't take `file`'s \"Intel i386\" / `pefile` machine names / the Go GOARCH token as the answer; the\n210\t  metadata field is the raw u16. And require `PE\\0\\0` exactly at e_lfanew -- an `MZ` stub alone is not a PE (decoy).\n211\t- Hex width (D10, cost a wrong submit + 17 s): `\"0x%x\"` drops leading zeros; print `0x%0{2*size}x` for the field's\n212\t  struct size. RVA vs VA: `_rva` = the raw field, never ImageBase + it.\n213\t- Fastest path for a new carry-over day: copy the previous day's solver (which already answers every earlier family) and\n214\t  add only the new suffix handler -- D8 27 s, D9 47 s that way. The harness skeleton in `solver/solve.py` is NOT the\n215\t  previous day's solver; `cp challenges/day<NN-1>/metadata-*/solver/solve.py` over it (D10 spliced by sed instead).\n216\t- Pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the HTTP 409 `start_required` body: `questions` (with ids, no sha tag) but\n217\t  NO `answer_ids` -- `jq '.answer_ids|map(..)'` errors; read `questions[].id` to preview the field set.\n218\t- Harness: re-running `hctf start` on an already-solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` and made the stop gate\n219\t  think it was incomplete (Day 2, ~2 min lost) — restore start.json from `log.jsonl`.\n220\t- Tools installed (2026-10-07): exiftool, pdfinfo/pdftotext (poppler), qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck,\n221\t  zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost, mediainfo, sqlite3, identify/convert (ImageMagick), olevba/oleid.\n222\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00ed06c6-0522-49a2-88e5-afcd48f88547","uuid":"175063e5-a454-4345-beeb-7041896d4ebc","timestamp":"2026-10-13T13:06:02.486Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md","content":"# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-12; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- Every day = ONE evidence zip (`metadata-day-NN-evidence.zip`, plain Deflate, no password so far). Days 1-7: one tiny\n  member (33 B - 3 KB) and ONE structural fact. Day 8+: the zip carries the whole cumulative kit (note + jpg + png + pdf +\n  inner zip [+ D9 a 1.26 MB PE `.exe`]) and even the SINGLE contract asks every field (D8 12, D9 13 = identity + every\n  earlier day's field + the new one). The member can itself be a container (D7/8: an inner ZIP whose own EOCD / CD is\n  the asked field). Each day adds ONE member + ONE field; the previous kit members are byte-identical except the case id.\n- Day 9 crossed into EXECUTABLE headers (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`): the metadata lane now parses binaries too, but only\n  the raw header field -- answer the u16 as hex, not the binary lane's machine word (`i386`). Day 10 stayed on the SAME\n  PE (`pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex`) and DE-escalated: zip = the exe only, contract = 1 field (TT 1, Mastery 2x1).\n  Day 11 kept that shape and moved INTO the PE's resources (`pe.version_original_filename`, VS_VERSIONINFO string).\n  Day 12 switched to a NEW member family -- a 5 KB .NET dll (`d12-dotnet-NNN-dotnet-mvid-guid`) -- and went into the CLI\n  METADATA tables (Module.Mvid via the #GUID heap); same 1-field / TT 1 / Mastery 2x1 shape.\n- A new `<fmt>.<field>` family each day: identity (name/size/hashes) -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` ->\n  `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` -> `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries` ->\n  `zip.central_directory_member_names` -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex` ->\n  `pe.version_original_filename` -> `dotnet.mvid_guid`. Since Day 3 the question literally names the field\n  (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); answer ids read `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`). NOTE the\n  `dNN` is the drop/member family, not the day the field appeared: Day 8's new field came as `d07-zip-001-zip-central-\n  directory-member-names`; Day 9's as `d09-pe-001-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex` (new member family -> new `dNN`); Day 10's as `d09-pe-001-pe-address-of-entry-point-rva-hex` (same exe family), Day 11's as\n  `d09-pe-001-pe-version-original-filename`, Day 12's as `d12-dotnet-001-dotnet-mvid-guid` (new family -> new `dNN`).\n- The prompt's flavor text describes decoys (impostors, renamed copies, \"-with-bom\" names, EXIF/presentation lies, chunk\n  \"passengers\", catalog /Version overrides, \"impossible provenance\" names). The asked field so far was always the\n  STRUCTURAL truth from the header/record bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. Singles D1-D9 were\n  first-submit CORRECT in ~27-60 s; D10 took one wrong spelling (unpadded hex). Every TT/Mastery since D4 CORRECT first try.\n- The flavor promises MORE than the sample delivers (D9: \"executables for several architectures, plus decoys wearing\n  executable extensions\" -> one honest i386 PE, no ELF/Mach-O/decoy in any mode). Expect the promised cases to arrive\n  later as mutations; pre-arm the sibling parsers (ELF/Mach-O/decoy -> `none`) without guessing their spellings.\n- Titles are puns, not format hints: Day 7 \"Seven-Zip, No Relation\" was plain ZIP (PKWARE), no .7z anywhere.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\" below; resolve the named member through whatever wrapper arrives.\n- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions/names, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree\n  with the header: always answer from the structural header bytes of the member the question names.\n- **Member and values** -- names, sizes, dimensions and counts re-roll per variant; nothing about the sample is\n  constant (Day 7 entry count went 2/3/4/5 with drop number 001-004; member names `room-NN/item-K.txt`). Day 8 re-rolled\n  ONLY the note's case id (`Case <hex> evidence note.`, 33 B) -> md5/sha1/sha256/magic differ per set; jpg 257x146, png\n  269x153, pdf 1.4, eocd 2, CD names identical across single/TT/5 Mastery sets. D9 same, plus the PE: Machine 0x014c in\n  all 7 copies but the exe's sha256 differs per set (re-built per variant). D10: the entry RVA re-rolled per variant\n  (single 0x00065bd0, TT 0x00063a80, Mastery 0x00063510 / 0x00065bd0). D11: the PE's ARCHITECTURE re-rolled per variant\n  (single 386 0x014c, TT amd64 0x8664, Mastery arm64 0xaa64 + 386) and OriginalFilename follows it (`pe-base-<goarch>.exe`).\n  D12: every dll is 5,120 B with the same layout; the MVID, the sha256 and the `Huntress.Managed.<12HEX>` type name re-roll\n  per variant (managed-001..004).\n  Never cache a value across sets.\n- **Field-set size** -- grows AND shrinks: D7 TT/Mastery went 1 -> 11 fields (Mastery 22); D8 12 in every mode (Mastery\n  5 x 12); D9 13 (Mastery 5 x 13); D10 back to ONE field everywhere (Mastery 2 sets x 1, zip = the lone exe). Families: the day's field +\n  `evidence-note-{filename,size-bytes,md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}` + carry-overs\n  `d04-jpeg-*-sof-dimensions-pixels`, `d05-png-*-ihdr-dimensions-pixels`, `d06-pdf-*-header-version`, `d07-zip-*-eocd-\n  total-entries`, `d07-zip-*-central-directory-member-names`, `d09-pe-*-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex`. Dispatch on the\n  answer-id SUFFIX and keep EVERY earlier family answerable (reference: `challenges/day09/metadata-built-different/\n  solver/solve.py` answers all 13; `day10/metadata-where-do-we-begin/solver/solve.py` = those + entry/image-base/opt-magic\n  /ELF e_entry branches).\n- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes, case-insensitive; D9 also `0x`-hex with `trim` only,\n  so case MATTERS -> lowercase), `enum` (`accepted_values`), and since D8 `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact\n  values and order\"). Emit per `answer_format.kind`; read `syntax` for prefix/case (`0x` yes for u16_hex, no for magic).\n- **Question-text tags** (D9 TT/Mastery, new): the first question gets ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<64 hex>]` appended\n  (Mastery: the bundle's sha, same for every set). Strip `\\s*\\[[^\\]]*\\]$` before reading a member name from question\n  text; route by `answer_id` + `artifact` instead (the D9 solver was unaffected for that reason).\n- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7: outer -> `...-evidence-0N.zip` ->\n  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer from an enclosing zip.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | `7z l -slt <zip>` then `7z x -o work/ <zip>`; (or python `zipfile` read of the member) |\n| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the extracted member (bytes, not the zip entry name) |\n| \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |\n| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM = `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`, UTF-32LE `ff fe 00 00`) -> `true`/`false` |\n| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk JPEG segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width. `exiftool -ImageSize` cross-check only |\n| `png.ihdr_*` / \"walk their chunks\" | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = IHDR width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC loop (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n| `zip.eocd_*` / \"count what the archives claim\" | of the NAMED inner zip (not the evidence zip): last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+8 disk entries, @+10 total, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset, u16 @+20 comment len. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 locator `PK\\x06\\x07` (EOCD-20) -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32. Cross-check: count `PK\\x01\\x02` walking from cd offset, `PK\\x03\\x04` |\n| `zip.central_directory_*` / \"inventory every stored path, preserve directory context\" | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from EOCD cd-offset (fallback `EOCD - cd_size` if data prepended): name len u16 @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name at +46; next = +46+n+e+c. Raw stored path, CD order, no basename/dedupe/sort; decode UTF-8 (flag bit 11 `0x800`, else try UTF-8 then cp437). `7z l -slt` / `zipinfo -1` as cross-check |\n| `pdf.header_version` / \"declared versions\" | `head -c 16 <f> | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; `grep -a -o '/Version[^/>]*'` only as a diagnostic |\n| `pe.coff_*` / \"executables for several architectures\", `.exe`/`.dll`/`.sys` | `MZ`@0 -> e_lfanew u32 LE @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` there -> COFF FileHeader: Machine u16 @+4, NumberOfSections @+6, TimeDateStamp @+8, SizeOfOptionalHeader @+20, Characteristics @+22; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b` PE32 / `0x20b` PE32+). `xxd -s $((0x3c)) -l 4` then `xxd -s <lfanew> -l 8`. `file`/`pefile` cross-check only |\n| `pe.address_of_entry_point_*` / `pe.image_base*` / \"start addresses\" | opt = e_lfanew+24: AddressOfEntryPoint u32 @opt+16 (an RVA); ImageBase u32 @opt+28 (PE32) / u64 @opt+24 (PE32+). `od -An -tx4 -j$((lfanew+40)) -N4 f`. objdump's \"start address\" = ImageBase+RVA (a VA, NOT the RVA) |\n| `elf.*` / `macho.*` siblings (promised \"several architectures\", not yet asked) | ELF: `\\x7fELF`, EI_DATA @5 picks endianness, e_machine u16 @18. Mach-O: `feedface`/`feedfacf` (either byte order) cputype u32 @4; fat `cafebabe` = BE nfat_arch @4 + 20-B entries (Java .class shares `cafebabe`; small nfat_arch = fat). Emit hex in the same `0x%0Nx` width as the field's `uNN` |\n| `dotnet.*` / `.dll` \"Mono/.Net assembly\" / \"module identities\", \"rebuilds vs renames\" | CLI metadata, stdlib only (no dnfile in-window): PE data dir 14 (CLI header) -> MetaData RVA -> `BSJB` root -> stream headers (`#~`, `#Strings`, `#GUID`, `#Blob`). `#~`: HeapSizes byte @+6 (bit1 = 4-byte GUID index), Valid u64 @+8, row counts @+24; Module row 0 = Generation u16, Name (str idx), **Mvid (guid idx, 1-based)** -> 16 B at #GUID+(i-1)*16 -> `str(uuid.UUID(bytes_le=..))`. Cross-check: `monodis`/`ilspycmd -il` print `.module` + `// MVID: {..}` |\n| `pe.version_*` / \"version resources remember what the binaries called themselves\" | VS_VERSIONINFO StringFileInfo: `pefile.PE(data=b, fast_load=True)`; `pe.parse_data_directories(directories=[DIRECTORY_ENTRY['IMAGE_DIRECTORY_ENTRY_RESOURCE']])`; walk `pe.FileInfo[..][..].StringTable[..].entries` (bytes keys). Match the id tail to the key ignoring case/`-_` (`original-filename` -> `OriginalFilename`). Shell: `strings -e l f.exe | grep -A1 OriginalFilename` |\n| exe-extension decoy (`.exe` that is text/zip/PNG, `MZ` with no/garbled `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | header absent -> literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit or the extension |\n| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n| answer_format syntax \"use the literal none only when the requested field is absent\" | field missing (e.g. no header) -> `none` |\n| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)` -- compact, no spaces, no Markdown |\n| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids, artifact `delivery N: <zip> -> <member>` or `<zip>-0N.zip -> <member>` | resolve each set's member separately; see delivery layouts below |\n\n## Day by day\n**Day 1 — You Must Be This Hash to Ride** (identity: filename / size-bytes / md5 / sha1 / sha256 via `zipfile` +\n`hashlib`; CORRECT ~36 s). Mastery zip-of-zips first seen.\n\n**Day 2 — Looks Can Be Deceiving** (`magic-prefix-hex-16`: first 16 bytes, lowercase hex, no `0x`; ~34 s). TT `readme.exe`\nwas text, Mastery `.bin` was a PDF. TT question text named a member that didn't exist -> `lib.common.find_artifact_hinted`;\nzip-of-zips broke name lookup -> `find_artifact` recurses nested zips.\n\n**Day 3 — BOM Voyage** (`text.utf8_bom_present` enum `true`/`false`). First 3 bytes == `EF BB BF`; CORRECT ~28 s.\nMastery `export-001-with-bom.txt` really had a BOM -- decide from bytes, never the name. utf16/32 variants unconfirmed.\n\n**Day 4 — Picture This** (`jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels`). Walk segments by declared length to SOFn (one SOF0 @0x88) ->\n`<width>x<height>` (GM-confirmed; not EXIF/filename dims). Rotation flavor not asked. CORRECT ~38 s; TT/Mastery in-window.\n\n**Day 5 — Chunk Norris** (`png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels`). IHDR @0x10 BE u32 width,height -> `<width>x<height>` (Day 4\nform by analogy, accepted). IDAT/CRC/after-IEND \"passenger\" checks were diagnostics only. CORRECT ~33 s, first try.\n\n**Day 6 — Portable Deception** (`pdf.header_version`): `xxd -l 16` -> `%PDF-1.4` -> bare `x.y` (~34 s). Adopted, not\nGM-judged: header must be at offset 0 (deeper `%PDF-` -> `none`); catalog `/Version` never changes it. Mastery: two\nsame-named downloads (`delivery N:` refs); pre-fetched contract listed 003/004, live asked 006/007.\n\n**Day 7 — Seven-Zip, No Relation** (`zip.eocd_total_entries` integer of the INNER `evidence-drop-001.zip`): EOCD u16\n@+10 = `2` (the claim; all variants honest, claim-vs-walk disagreement never exercised). Stdlib `struct` EOCD parser,\n57 s first try; TT 3 entries, Mastery 4 / 5.\n\n**Day 8 — What's in the Box?** (`zip.central_directory_member_names`, kind `json`): 5-member kit (note/jpg/png/pdf/D7\ninner zip), single = 12 fields. Inner zip's CD names verbatim in CD order, full paths (basenames collide):\n`[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]`, compact JSON. \"Impossible provenance\" decoy unexercised. ~27 s first try.\n\n**Day 9 — Built Different** (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`, `pattern` lowercase `0x`): kit + `telemetry-agent-001.exe`, an\nhonest Go 1.22 386 PE32 (e_lfanew 0x80, 7 sections, opt magic 0x10b). COFF Machine u16 -> `0x014c` (padded; not `i386`,\nthe binary lane's word). \"Several architectures + decoys\" flavor unexercised. ~47 s first try; TT/Mastery 5 x 13 in-window.\n\n**Day 10 — Where Do We Begin?** (`pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex`, id `d09-pe-001-...`): zip = the D9 Go 386 PE\nalone, 1 field everywhere. OptionalHeader.AddressOfEntryPoint (u32 @ e_lfanew+40) `0x%08x` -> `0x00065bd0`; unpadded\n`0x65bd0` REJECTED (lane's first wrong submit). objdump's start address is the VA, not the RVA. ~75 s, 1 wrong; TT/Mastery\nfirst try (RVA re-rolled per variant). \"Lying report\" flavour unexercised.\n\n**Day 11 — What's My Name Again?** (`pe.version_original_filename`, id `d09-pe-001-pe-version-original-filename`): same\nlone Go PE; VS_VERSIONINFO OriginalFilename VERBATIM (`pe-base-386.exe`), not the randomized member name\n(`telemetry-agent-001.exe` = the \"impersonator\"). pefile resource walk, ONE command, ~25 s first try; TT amd64 / Mastery\narm64 + 386 variants, both first try.\n\n**Day 12 — Managed Expectations** (`dotnet.mvid_guid`, kind `pattern`, syntax \"canonical GUID text in 8-4-4-4-12\nhexadecimal form, including hyphens\", norm `trim`, id `d12-dotnet-001-dotnet-mvid-guid`). Prompt: \"The .NET assemblies\nshare names, versions, and source ancestry -- but their module identities remain distinct. Separate rebuilds from renames.\"\n- Artifact: 2 KB zip -> `managed-001.dll`, 5,120 B PE32 i386 .NET (BSJB `v4.0.30319`; `<Module>`, a\n  `Huntress.Managed.<12HEX>` type and a `get_ModuleVersionId` memberref -- the hint). One dll per delivery; the \"renames vs\n  rebuilds\" comparison was never asked, only the MVID.\n- Key insight: MVID = Module table row 0, 3rd column (guid-heap index, 1-based) -> 16 bytes in `#GUID` rendered as .NET\n  `Guid.ToString()` = mixed-endian (`uuid.UUID(bytes_le=...)`), lowercase, no braces: `21e410f3-c977-465c-80eb-6890ddd3085c`.\n- Worker: the solver was the bare skeleton; it typed a ~90-line stdlib PE -> CLI header -> BSJB streams -> `#~` -> `#GUID`\n  parser + the old identity/PE branches and submitted in ONE command (2 tool calls; most of the ~55 s launch->CORRECT was\n  generation). First try. Reference parser: `challenges/day12/metadata-managed-expectations/solver/solve.py` `dotnet_mvid`.\n- TT window 30 s, in_window 0.95 s (managed-002); Mastery 2 sets (003/004), in_window 1.5 s. Both CORRECT first try.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`).\n- Booleans: enum `true` / `false` (lowercase) — the contract hands the vocabulary; pick, don't probe.\n- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR): `<width>x<height>` — width first, lowercase `x`, no spaces (GM-confirmed both,\n  re-confirmed D8 `257x146` / `269x153`).\n- PDF header version: bare `x.y` from the leading `%PDF-x.y` (no `PDF-`/`%` prefix); absent header -> literal `none`\n  (contract wording; `none` itself not yet GM-confirmed).\n- Counts (`zip.eocd_total_entries`): plain base-10 integer string, e.g. `2` (GM-confirmed D7 + D8 all modes).\n- JSON lists (`zip.central_directory_member_names`): compact array, no spaces after `,`, double quotes, full stored path\n  with `/` dirs, CD order -- `[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]` (GM-confirmed D8 single/TT/Mastery x5).\n  Whether the GM's `trim` normalization also tolerates `\", \"` spacing is untested -- always emit compact.\n- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 Machine ->\n  `0x014c` (D9), u32 AddressOfEntryPoint -> `0x00065bd0` (D10, all modes). The width comes from the STRUCT, not the id\n  (D10's id has no `u32`). Contrast: magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; binary-lane `machine` wants the word (`i386`), and the\n  binary lane's `entry_point` was accepted UNPADDED (`0x401040`) -- different lane, different generator.\n- GUIDs (`dotnet.mvid_guid`): .NET `Guid.ToString()` form -- first 3 groups byte-swapped from the heap bytes (bytes_le),\n  lowercase, hyphenated, no braces (D12 all modes; `knowledge.DOTNET_MVID_GUID`, playbook metadata `guid` entry).\n- Version-resource strings (`pe.version_<field>`): the StringFileInfo value verbatim, incl. extension (`pe-base-386.exe`,\n  D11 all modes). `knowledge.PE_VERSION_STRING_KEY` maps id tail -> resource key.\n- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` for pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex (D10 single; unpadded) -- the only one, days 1-12.\n- `knowledge.py`: `JPEG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PNG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PDF_HEADER_VERSION_FMT`, `ZIP_EOCD_TOTAL_ENTRIES_FMT`,\n  `ZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_FMT`, `PE_COFF_MACHINE_U16_HEX_FMT`, `PE_ENTRY_POINT_RVA_HEX_FMT` (+`_REJECTED`), `BOOL`;\n  `playbook` metadata `hex` entry carries the padding rule.\n- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_dimensions_pixels` = SOF frame header, `ihdr_` = IHDR chunk,\n  `header_version` = file header, `eocd_total_entries` = EOCD record's own claim, `central_directory_member_names` = CD\n  file-name fields, `coff_machine_u16_hex` = COFF FileHeader.Machine as u16 hex) — read the field name literally to\n  pick which structure to parse; a claimed count is NOT a CD walk / `zipfile` len, and CD names are NOT local-header\n  names (they happened to agree on D7/D8). A `_uNN_hex` suffix fixes both the read width and the printed width.\n\n## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (D8: 5 members, filename question's artifact = zip only).\n- Mastery days 1,2,4,5: ONE download named `...-evidence-01.zip` that is an outer zip containing `...-01.zip` and\n  `...-02.zip` (zip-of-zips); each inner zip holds its set's member.\n- Mastery day 7: zip-of-zips again, three levels (outer `-01.zip` holds `-01.zip` + `-02.zip`, each holding the asked\n  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); artifact ref `metadata-day-07-evidence-0N.zip -> evidence-drop-00N.zip` (no `delivery N:`).\n- Mastery day 8: same shape, FIVE sets: one 17 KB download `metadata-day-08-evidence-01.zip` (Stored, UTF-8 flag) holding\n  `-01.zip`..`-05.zip`, each a full 5-member kit (incl. its own `evidence-drop-001.zip`). Refs `...-evidence-0N.zip ->\n  <member>`; every set reuses the same member names, so resolve by (set zip, member), never member name alone.\n- Mastery day 9: same five-set shape, but the GM download is named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip`\n  (`metadata-forensics-day-09-built-different-mastery.zip`, 2.99 MB, Stored) while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip\n  -> <member>` -- resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not by its filename.\n- Mastery day 10: TWO sets only, refs `metadata-day-10-evidence-0N.zip -> telemetry-agent-00N.exe` (003/004).\n  Day 11 identical shape (`metadata-day-11-evidence-0N.zip`, one download nesting both set zips).\n- Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` in artifact refs.\n- Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) — never hardcode names.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- Name lookup by zip filename alone breaks on zip-of-zips (returned `PK` bytes as the \"magic\") — recurse into nested zips.\n- Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (Day 2 TT): answer under `answer_ids`, locate the member that exists.\n- Don't let the flavor text widen the question: prompts mention impostors/passengers/orientation/provenance, but only the\n  named field is graded. Answer it; keep extra checks as diagnostics.\n- Container-of-containers: when the asked file is itself a zip, a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded evidence\n  zip reads the OUTER EOCD / CD (D8 outer CD = the 5 kit members, Mastery outer = 5 set zips). Resolve the named member's\n  bytes first, then parse.\n- Name-list fields: `zipfile.namelist()` is CD order but decodes non-UTF-8-flagged names as cp437 and is fine for honest\n  zips; for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `C:\\`, `\\` separators, LFH != CD name, duplicates) emit the CD bytes as-is --\n  don't let an extractor's sanitizing (7z/unzip strip `../` and leading `/`) rewrite the answer.\n- Decoys by name: `*-with-bom.txt`, `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF, `.pdf` that is PNG — bytes win every time.\n- Timed windows are ~5-10 s (D8: TT 8 s / Mastery 10 s; D9 shrank to 6 s / 7 s) and most of it is GM start/download/\n  submit round-trips (D9 TT submit alone 2.3 s): never do anything slow (extraction to disk, exiftool, `pefile` full\n  parse, subprocess) in-window; parse fixed offsets in memory. Big members (1.2 MB exe x5) pushed Mastery solve to 0.86 s\n  -- decompress each member once and cache by (set zip, member).\n- Fresh member family = skeleton solver (D10, D12): copy the previous day's solver first, then add the new family's\n  handler -- D12's worker re-typed the identity/PE branches next to the .NET parser (~50 s of generation).\n- Executable fields: don't take `file`'s \"Intel i386\" / `pefile` machine names / the Go GOARCH token as the answer; the\n  metadata field is the raw u16. And require `PE\\0\\0` exactly at e_lfanew -- an `MZ` stub alone is not a PE (decoy).\n- Hex width (D10, cost a wrong submit + 17 s): `\"0x%x\"` drops leading zeros; print `0x%0{2*size}x` for the field's\n  struct size. RVA vs VA: `_rva` = the raw field, never ImageBase + it.\n- Fastest path for a new carry-over day: copy the previous day's solver (which already answers every earlier family) and\n  add only the new suffix handler -- D8 27 s, D9 47 s that way. The harness skeleton in `solver/solve.py` is NOT the\n  previous day's solver; `cp challenges/day<NN-1>/metadata-*/solver/solve.py` over it (D10 spliced by sed instead).\n- Pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the HTTP 409 `start_required` body: `questions` (with ids, no sha tag) but\n  NO `answer_ids` -- `jq '.answer_ids|map(..)'` errors; read `questions[].id` to preview the field set.\n- Harness: re-running `hctf start` on an already-solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` and made the stop gate\n  think it was incomplete (Day 2, ~2 min lost) — restore start.json from `log.jsonl`.\n- Tools installed (2026-10-07): exiftool, pdfinfo/pdftotext (poppler), qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck,\n  zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost, mediainfo, sqlite3, identify/convert (ImageMagick), olevba/oleid.\n","numLines":222,"startLine":1,"totalLines":222}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Bvw24ZCpgSq7x2hvTVkd5F","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
