{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzHYNqj4DfV6WHokftFy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Day 13 needed no new work. The carried-forward solver answered the single solve, the time trial and mastery correctly on the first submit, with no worker reasoning and no solver edits.\n\n**1. Artifact and new questions**\n- `evidence.zip` (98,779 B, sha256 `08092cc8…7ba2`) is a flat zip of 105 members, all AES-encrypted (compress_type 99). Mastery was an outer `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01.zip` and `evidence-02.zip` (2 sets × 913 = 1826 answers).\n- 913 questions; day 12's contract had 855, so 58 are new and none were removed. Everything else repeats earlier days (ps1 samples, jscript/batch/vbs/python/bash/node graphs, polyglot php/lua/wmi_mof/typescript, host-* files).\n- New family A, `polyglot-applescript-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}` (4 × 11 = 44 ids). Members are `polyglot-applescript-*.applescript`. Fields: role, attack, adapter, campaign, file-path|url, stage-count, steps, host-profile, obfuscation, stage-profile, next-language.\n- New family B, `bash-advanced-{subshell-pipeline,process-substitution}` (2 × 7 = 14 ids), from `subshell-pipeline.sh` and `process-substitution.sh`. Fields: role, attack, feature, primitive, campaign, stage-count, steps.\n\n**2. Key insight**\nBoth new families use encodings the generic decoder already handled:\n- AppleScript files start with `-- HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<payload>` (tags seen: HB64, FRAG, HEX), with the same payload repeated in `property descriptor_xxx : \"...\"`. The decoded plan is `v=3|language=applescript|role=...|obfuscation_profile=...`.\n- The new bash files use the day 7 advanced-syntax layout: `Material_<id>` hex plus `Codec_<id>='hex_compact|'`, decoding to `v=1|feature=..|primitive=..|campaign_id=..|stage_count=..|steps=..`.\n\n**3. What ran**\nThe orchestrator's probe ran the unchanged `solver/solve.py --contrac