obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>='..'` + `readonly Codec_<id>='rep|transform|key'` | Decode from the Codec const (key hex; multi-byte key = COMMA list). Re-join split/`+=`/adjacent-quoted chunks. Never run bash. |\n| `.sh` with `Feature_<id>()` (`${!pointer}`, `local -a parts=('cu' 'rl')`, `local -A`, `${arr[@]:1:2}`, `trap 'return 0' RETURN`, a self-calling `walk_fixture`), plan `v=1|feature=..|primitive=..` | Role `advanced_syntax` (closed enum value). feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps are plan-verbatim; attack = T1059.004. The `Feature_` body is the feature; never name it from the code, copy the plan. |\n| `.mjs` ESM: `const Material_<id> = \"..\"; const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>`, `process.env.HUNTRESS_INSPECT_ONLY` | Static decode with `lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback (reps hex_buffer, hex_array, escaped_octets `\\\\xNN`, decimal_array, unicode_escapes, json_numbers). Don't run it (top-level await, Buffer/vm). Plan fields verbatim; role from `steps`. |\n| `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` or `-- HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` + `descriptor_<id> = \"..\"` (`.php`; `.lua` `local descriptor_..` + `build_plan_<id>`, OpenResty `inert_handler_<id>` returning `{status=200,..}`; `.js` that is really HTA `<hta:application>`, WSF `<job><script language=\"JScript\">` or SCT `<?xml?><scriptlet><registration progid=..>` CDATA; `.vbs` that is a WSF job; `.au3` AutoIt `; HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:` + `Global Const $descriptor_..`) | **Route by the marker, before the extension** (the extension lies). Peel the descriptor by shape to `v=3|language=..|role=..|verdict=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer, including role and attack, is plan-verbatim. Python `-I` + base64/bytes.fromhex is enough. |\n| Real `.pyc` / PyInstaller / pyarmor (not seen yet) | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)` (pyinstxtractor-ng + decompyle3, `dis` fallback). See skills/script-analysis. |\n| Any `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` | A hex byte, not text. Transforms are named for the ENCODE side: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING, `add_modulo_256` by SUBTRACTING. `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte, seeded with the key. |\n\n## Day by day\n**D1 Power Play (PS, 15)**: base64 JSON descriptors. Collection ATT&CK cost 5 wrong before `T1555.003` (tell: `Login\nData`/`Cookies`). **Map the SPECIFIC artifact, not the generic tactic.** ~15 min.\n**D2 Host With the Most (+JScript, 87)**: plans behind base64/XOR/reverse/byte-shift, eval'd by `inspect_*`; node `vm` +\neval capture. Handoff = `staged_chain` (`relay` REJECTED). 7 wrong, all ATT&CK guesses. ~22 min.\n**D3 Expansion Pack (+Batch, 159): the costly day, ~1 h 45 min, ~127 rejected probes.** expansion/control are GM labels,\nnot surface reading; `if defined X` burned ~40 synonyms before `if_guard` -> NAMING LAWS.\n**D4 Dim and Dimmer (+VBScript, 231)**: Codec const + small VBS interpreter; control probed one field at a time. 4 wrong, ~7 min.\n**D5 Hatch Careful (+Python, 357)**: `*-recovered.py` source, plan v=2 gave every label. 0 wrong, ~4 min.\n**D6 Shell We Begin (+Bash, 399)**: stage-count = plan stage_count (NOT len(steps)); steps `>`-joined. 0 wrong, ~4 min.\n**D7 Node by Node (+Node `.mjs` + 2 Bash advanced, 469)**: same Material_/Codec_ pattern in ESM; new roles\npersistence_descriptor (T1053.003) and advanced_syntax (T1059.004). 469/469 first submit, ~100 s. TT: attempt 5ab8013f\nmissed 15 ids (new reps unicode_escapes/json_numbers/`xor_hex|cd`); 26b7da83 saved `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` as the zip;\n3rd CORRECT. Mastery CORRECT first try. Lesson: **diagnose EVERY failed attempt, not only the latest.**\n**D8 Lost in Translation (+8 PHP polyglot, +4 host formats, +2 Bash advanced; 615)**: new files carry the v=3 plan\n(`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` + `descriptor_<id>`, byte-identical); role/attack/adapter/profiles stated, **copy, don't\nderive**. New fields host-profile, obfuscation, stage-profile, next-language. ~2 min 10 s, 2 submits, 0 wrong (6 ids lost\nto hyphenated family names -> longest-known-suffix field parse). TT 2.1 s / Mastery 5.6 s in-window, both 1st try.\n\n**D9 All the World's a Stager (+4 Lua polyglot, +2 hosts SCT/OpenResty, +2 Bash advanced; 695)** and **D10 Bind Over Matter\n(+4 WMI MOF polyglot, +2 Bash advanced; 753)**: v=3 marker in `--` / `//` comments; flavour (\"impossible family tree\",\n\"subscription that survives a reboot\") unasked. The marker-routed solver answered both unchanged, 0 wrong, all modes 1st try.\n\n**D11 By Any Other Name (+4 TypeScript polyglot, +2 Bash advanced; 811 ids, 95 members)**: prompt \"These scripts reach for\nnative APIs by name, but a name isn't a behavior. Map each reference to the receipt-backed action it models, and flag the call\nwhose claimed purpose the evidence doesn't support.\" Flavour only: no flag/mismatch question; the PS samples' `$nativeTypes`\nscenario mapping is unchanged.\n- New: `polyglot-typescript-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}.ts` -- `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:` FRAG / HEX / B64 /\n  HB64 (obfuscation fragmented_hex / plain_hex / base64 / hex_base64), host_profile standalone, adapters local_parser /\n  http_client / process_builder / operation_graph, next_language powershell / jscript / batch / vbscript; attack none / T1105 /\n  T1059 / T1059 (V3 table). Steps again don't predict role (TS downloader = `decode_configuration>return_configuration`).\n- New Bash advanced: `nameref-dispatch.sh` (feature nameref_dispatch, primitive declare_nameref, `local -n`) and\n  `dynamic-file-descriptor.sh` (dynamic_file_descriptor, allocated_file_descriptor); `Material_` decimal CSV, `Codec_='decimal_csv|'`.\n- Method: the carried-over solver (marker-routed v=3 + suffix field parse) answered 811/811 unchanged; the worker cat'ed the\n  new files, ran the solver, grepped the new ids, submitted. 5 tool calls, launch 01:55:40Z -> CORRECT 01:56:35Z (~55 s, 0 wrong).\n- TT f99ea9ec (9 s window) 1.41 s in-window; Mastery 2d722b36 (11 s, 2 sets) 1.69 s (solve 0.81 s). Both CORRECT first try.\n\n**D12 AutoIt Takes Two (+4 AutoIt polyglot; 855 ids, 99 members)**: prompt \"Two inert AutoIt workflows arrived as a matched\nset, and each one carries half the story. Correlate them ... decide which pairing is genuine\". Flavour only: no pairing /\ngenuine-vs-decoy question; the 4 new files are ordinary v=3 fixtures.\n- New: `polyglot-autoit-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}.au3` -- `; HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` comment +\n  `Global Const $descriptor_<id> = \"<hex>\"`; campaign `AUTOIT-<8hex>`, file_path `/tmp/huntress-autoit/.<16hex>.stage`, url\n  `https://autoit-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`. Role/attack per the V3 table (none / T1105 / T1059 / T1059); obfuscation\n  plain_hex / base64 / hex_base64 / fragmented_hex, next_language powershell / jscript / batch / vbscript, host_profile\n  standalone -- the exact D11 TypeScript set in a new host syntax.\n- Method: the carried-over solver's marker regex (comment-syntax agnostic) covered `;` comments: 855/855, no code change.\n  Launch -> CORRECT ~25 s (worker only cat'ed one `.au3`), 0 wrong. TT 30 s window, in_window 7.19 s (SUBMIT 5.33 s of it --\n  GM latency on 855 ids, not solve); Mastery 2 sets / 1710 ids, 4.04 s. Both CORRECT first try.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` gives the list (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.\n- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly):","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EfwVTffSr2kpmxyyC2MLXe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"con