{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzHnEAxnmd68MrYwY2yp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I finished the Day 13 ratchet. All five checks passed after the last lib edit: `test_orchestrate` (24/24), `test_day6_fixes`, `test_day7_fixes`, `test_codec` and `lib.refs.coverage 13` (100%, first try).\n\n1. **lib, MSI ProductCode:** I checked the metadata worker's proposal against `submissions.jsonl`: the bare GUID was rejected, and the braced uppercase `{DD1A80D5-…}` was accepted in the single solve, Time Trial and both Mastery sets. I added it to `lib/knowledge.py` as `MSI_PRODUCT_CODE_GUID`, with a `_REJECTED` list holding the bare form. I also widened the existing metadata `guid` rule in `lib/playbook.py` to say a GUID is spelled the way its source stores it, whatever the answer format text says. I kept that as one rule because the lookup only ever returns the first entry for a family, so a second `guid` entry would never be used. I also recorded Crystal's confirmed `hcfg_offset` (560188, where the base64 text starts) as another example of the base64-offset rule.\n2. **lib, Atbash:** `lib.decode.decode_chunk` now has a small Atbash branch, which is only picked when it scores better as English than both the best ROT-N and the reversed text. It now decodes the Day 13 single-solve blob to the confirmed slug. Across all historic warmups case blobs, the 690 from Days 1–12 decode exactly as before, and every warmups solver from Day 1 to Day 13 still passes all its cases. I added a one-line check to `tests/test_day7_fixes.py`.\n3. **Technique logs:** I added Day 13 entries to all five lane logs and updated the overview, recognition-cue and pitfall sections:\n   - **Warmups:** the rejected ROT-N-of-Atbash slug, plus a new variant axis. Mastery blobs now mix ROT-N, reversed and Atbash lines, and they have to be assigned together with each transform used once (the solver's `_joint`).\n   - **Metadata:** reading an MSI's Property table, plus a pitfall about stripping braces from a stored value.\n   - **Binary:** the Crystal runtime fingerprint and how its String literal is laid out.\n   - **Scripting:** the new AppleScript `property descriptor_` syntax.\n   - **Mobile:** \"keystore misuse\" was only a label; the dex has no crypto code.\n\n   I compressed older entries to keep the logs short (metadata Days 1–8, scripting D9–D12).\n4. **Rejected or left out:**\n   - The joint Mastery assignment stays in the Day 13 warmups solver. It is a whole-blob search, not \"one small branch\", so the log points to it instead.\n   - Nothing went into `lib/codec.py`. Day 13 scripting needed no new encoding, and its solver files are identical to Day 12's.\n   - Mobile and binary needed no lib changes, since both carried-over solvers answered first try.\n   - I didn't pull the binary solver's older `fast_aes_unzip` proposal or the scripting solver's `gm_error_body`/`iter_entries` proposals into lib. They are carried over from earlier days, they are solver code rather than confirmed facts, and there was no Day 13 evidence for them.\n5. **Not touched:** I made no GM calls and didn't edit `hctf/`, `skills/` or `bin/`. Two small leftovers in the challenge folders, which I left alone: the binary solver's `NOTES.md` is still headed \"binary-swift-justice\", and the scripting solver's `_LEAF_EXT` doesn't list `.applescript`/`.lua`/`.mof`/`.ts`. That second one only costs a little speed, and I noted it in the scripting log."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1410,"cache_read_input_tokens":148417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1410},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00ed06c6-0522-49a2-88e5-afcd48f8854